      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "s1",
          "text": "Heat oven to 190C/fan 170C/gas 5. Butter two 20cm sandwich tins and line with non-stick baking paper.",
          "ingredientRefs": []
        },
        {
          "id": "s2",
          "text": "In a large bowl, beat 200g caster sugar, 200g softened butter, 4 beaten eggs, 200g self-raising flour, 1 tsp baking powder and 2 tbsp milk together until you have a smooth, soft batter.",
          "ingredientRefs": []
        },
        {
          "id": "s3",
          "text": "Divide the mixture between the tins, smooth the surface with a spatula or the back of a spoon.",
          "ingredientRefs": []
        },
        {
          "id": "s4",
          "text": "Bake for about 20 mins until golden and the cake springs back when pressed.",
          "ingredientRefs": []
        },
        {
          "id": "s5",
          "text": "Turn onto a cooling rack and leave to cool completely.",
          "ingredientRefs": []
        },
        {
          "id": "s6",
          "text": "To make the filling, beat the 100g softened butter until smooth and creamy, then gradually beat in 140g sifted icing sugar and a drop of vanilla extract (if you’re using it).",
          "ingredientRefs": []
        },
        {
          "id": "s7",
          "text": "Spread the buttercream over the bottom of one of the sponges. Top it with 170g strawberry jam and sandwich the second sponge on top.",
          "ingredientRefs": []
        },
        {
          "id": "s8",
          "text": "Dust with a little icing sugar before serving. Keep in an airtight container and eat within 2 days.",
          "ingredientRefs": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
